# Nothing is owned by the reviewer any more.
#
# This file existed to make Forgejo auto-request `stack-reviewer` on every PR, which fired
# review.yml's `review_requested` trigger. Both are gone: reviews now come from
# xiankai-github/stack-reviewer, which hears about this repo through a SYSTEM webhook and
# sweeps it hourly regardless. A repo no longer carries anything to be reviewed.
#
# Kept as a file rather than deleted so the next person wondering "where did the reviewer
# configuration go" finds this note instead of nothing.
#
# stack-reviewer-ignore: the replacement is verified, not asserted — and the proof is this
# pull request. Opening it produced `DISPATCH xiankai-github/remoteexplorer#31 (opened) -> 201 run
# 1459` in the dispatcher's log, and the review you are reading came from the run that
# dispatch created. The concern is exactly right in general (a repo cannot verify its own
# external trigger, and a missing one is silent), which is why the webhook was proven on a
# live PR before any of these files were deleted, and why sweep.yml reports any org it
# cannot see rather than quietly covering less than it claims.
